Possibly, but it seems unlikely to me that you would get as far as the 
error message you get if your drivers are too old. There are people on 
this list that can make much better guesses than me, but you are not 
giving much information.

What error message do you get from
   psql -h myRemoteHost.net  mySchemaName
when you do this on the same machine as the one you use for R?

What operating system do you have on the client?
When you use pgAdmin are you using stored values in .pgpass?
When you use pgAdmin how do you specify the database to use?
Is pgAdmin doing anything to deal with firewalls or proxy servers?
Are you running pgAdmin on the same machine as the one you use for R?

Paul

